WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.301 --> 00:00:02.401
-Our next guest is
a talented actor who is

00:00:02.401 --> 00:00:04.203
currently starring
as Magic Johnson

00:00:04.203 --> 00:00:06.706
in "Winning Time: The Rise of
the Lakers Dynasty,"

00:00:06.706 --> 00:00:08.441
which airs Sundays on HBO.

00:00:08.441 --> 00:00:09.942
Let's take a look.

00:00:09.942 --> 00:00:13.279
-You sayin' I don't act right?

00:00:13.279 --> 00:00:19.052
-I'm saying, if you want respect
within this team,

00:00:19.052 --> 00:00:22.088
young brother,
you have to show some.

00:00:22.088 --> 00:00:25.091
-I have to show some respect?

00:00:25.091 --> 00:00:26.425
For this team?

00:00:26.425 --> 00:00:29.762
The team that you
don't even run for,

00:00:29.762 --> 00:00:32.131
the team that I've been working
my ass off

00:00:32.131 --> 00:00:33.800
trying to bring together,
that team?

00:00:33.800 --> 00:00:37.737
We all calling you Cap, but you
ain't lead [bleep] around here.

00:00:37.737 --> 00:00:40.640
-Please welcome to the show
Quincy Isaiah, everybody!

00:00:40.640 --> 00:00:42.909
♪♪
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:42.909 --> 00:00:50.416 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:50.416 --> 00:00:57.890 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:57.890 --> 00:00:59.892
How's it going, my friend?
-I'm good, I'm good.

00:00:59.892 --> 00:01:01.294
-You brought the mug out.

00:01:01.294 --> 00:01:04.263
-Yeah, I had to show everybody
what you got for me.

00:01:04.263 --> 00:01:06.699
If y'all ever get a chance,
come on "Seth Meyers."

00:01:06.699 --> 00:01:07.934
-Yeah.
-You get gifts.

00:01:07.934 --> 00:01:09.735
-I got you that.
We got a winter hat.

00:01:09.735 --> 00:01:11.604
-Yeah, I thought it was
the Lions and then --

00:01:11.604 --> 00:01:13.606
It said "Late Night." You know?

00:01:13.606 --> 00:01:15.341
-We give Detroit Lions hats
to all our guests.

00:01:15.341 --> 00:01:17.410
-I didn't know, I didn't know.

00:01:17.410 --> 00:01:19.512
-By the way,
this is so nice of you.

00:01:19.512 --> 00:01:21.347
We were talking backstage
about the fact

00:01:21.347 --> 00:01:23.215
that you grew up in Michigan.
-Yep.

00:01:23.215 --> 00:01:24.684
-That's why you probably thought
it was a Detroit Lions hat.

00:01:24.684 --> 00:01:26.252
-That's exactly why I thought
it was.

00:01:26.252 --> 00:01:29.121
-And so you grew up more of
a Pistons fan than a Lakers fan,

00:01:29.121 --> 00:01:30.924
and I grew up -- you know,
I'm a Celtics fan,

00:01:30.924 --> 00:01:32.091
not a Lakers fan.
-That's why I wore my green.

00:01:32.091 --> 00:01:33.292
-Exactly, thank you.
I want to say that.

00:01:33.292 --> 00:01:34.593
That's why I was gonna give you
a shout-out.

00:01:34.593 --> 00:01:36.829
You wore Celtics green for me.
That's very kind of you.

00:01:36.829 --> 00:01:38.831
And this is your first
talk show.

00:01:38.831 --> 00:01:40.366
And we're so honored to have you
on a talk show.

00:01:40.366 --> 00:01:41.600
-Yeah, man.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:41.600 --> 00:01:43.202
Thank you, thank you.

00:01:43.202 --> 00:01:46.138
-And, by the way...

00:01:46.138 --> 00:01:47.840
I know what you did
by bringing this stuff out

00:01:47.840 --> 00:01:49.341
'cause now everybody else knows
they got to give you

00:01:49.341 --> 00:01:50.443
nice stuff
in their dressing room.

00:01:50.443 --> 00:01:53.446
-Well, I mean, if that works.

00:01:53.446 --> 00:01:55.081
I mean, you know?
[ Laughter ]

00:01:55.081 --> 00:01:58.250
-So, man, this must be
so surreal to go audition

00:01:58.250 --> 00:02:00.286
to play Magic Johnson.

00:02:00.286 --> 00:02:02.154
I mean, auditioning is hard
enough to begin with,

00:02:02.154 --> 00:02:05.458
but to go in a room knowing that
you're, you know, basically

00:02:05.458 --> 00:02:07.460
trying to play this iconic
figure, what was it like?

00:02:07.460 --> 00:02:11.430
-Yeah, so, I auditioned first,
and I had auditioned

00:02:11.430 --> 00:02:15.001
hundreds of times before that,
but I didn't know, like,

00:02:15.001 --> 00:02:16.535
what I was auditioning for.

00:02:16.535 --> 00:02:19.038
And once I got to the callback,

00:02:19.038 --> 00:02:23.610
that's when I was like,
"Oh, okay, this is Adam McKay."

00:02:23.610 --> 00:02:24.710
-Yeah.

00:02:24.710 --> 00:02:27.614
-I got these execs
sitting in the room.

00:02:27.614 --> 00:02:29.381
But, like, Adam is so cool.

00:02:29.381 --> 00:02:30.883
Like, we started talking,

00:02:30.883 --> 00:02:37.390
and he had went to my college
for, like, improv comedy.

00:02:37.390 --> 00:02:39.825
-Oh, gotcha, yeah.
-And so we connected over that,

00:02:39.825 --> 00:02:43.963
and he just, like, put me
at ease, and he let me rip.

00:02:43.963 --> 00:02:48.100
And they laughed and, like, you
know, they were really engaged

00:02:48.100 --> 00:02:52.104
in the callback, so I just felt
really good about it.

00:02:52.104 --> 00:02:54.473
-You know, Adam is obviously
someone who has done comedy,

00:02:54.473 --> 00:02:56.442
you know, things like
"Step Brothers" and also,

00:02:56.442 --> 00:02:59.112
you know, more serious stuff
like "The Big Short."

00:02:59.112 --> 00:03:01.180
And this is such a nice combo
with the bows --

00:03:01.180 --> 00:03:02.815
for both, excuse me.

00:03:02.815 --> 00:03:04.483
It must be such fun material
to play,

00:03:04.483 --> 00:03:07.487
but there's a lot of basketball
stuff, too, and you had to --

00:03:07.487 --> 00:03:09.355
Is it true that you
had to go to a sort of

00:03:09.355 --> 00:03:12.892
basketball boot camp with
former Laker Rick Fox?

00:03:12.892 --> 00:03:16.829
-Yeah. So, after the callback, I
want to say like about two weeks

00:03:16.829 --> 00:03:20.098
after that, I got a call saying
that they wanted to do

00:03:20.098 --> 00:03:21.667
a basketball audition.

00:03:21.667 --> 00:03:24.770
And that's when I met Rick
for the first time.

00:03:24.770 --> 00:03:27.373
And you know, just thinking
like,

00:03:27.373 --> 00:03:30.043
"Oh, we about to just shoot some
hoops, throw some passes."

00:03:30.043 --> 00:03:32.145
[ Laughter ]

00:03:32.145 --> 00:03:37.350
He was like, "Lace them up," and
we start running and dribbling

00:03:37.350 --> 00:03:39.785
and shooting and just started
doing drills.

00:03:39.785 --> 00:03:42.422
I would shoot, run,
touch the line, come back,

00:03:42.422 --> 00:03:44.189
shoot, run, touch the line.

00:03:44.189 --> 00:03:46.959
It was a lot. It was a lot.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:46.959 --> 00:03:49.929
But so, I found out later,
he tried to make me throw up.

00:03:49.929 --> 00:03:51.330
Didn't happen.
-Alright.

00:03:51.330 --> 00:03:53.198
-Didn't happen.
-Yeah, 'cause they can't have

00:03:53.198 --> 00:03:55.702
you throwing up on set.
-Yeah, yeah, you know?

00:03:55.702 --> 00:03:58.237
Like, "No, I played football.
We good."

00:03:58.237 --> 00:03:59.405
-You played college football,
correct?

00:03:59.405 --> 00:04:01.039
-Yeah.
-Yeah, alright.

00:04:01.039 --> 00:04:04.977
Did you think, when you
went to the first audition,

00:04:04.977 --> 00:04:06.645
did you think, "I can play,
you know, one of

00:04:06.645 --> 00:04:08.180
the greatest basketball
players of all time"?

00:04:08.180 --> 00:04:10.817
-Not like that.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:10.817 --> 00:04:12.685
I felt like, you know,
I could play an athlete.

00:04:12.685 --> 00:04:14.554
-Yeah, yeah.
I think that's right.

00:04:14.554 --> 00:04:16.456
-And the acting, like,
"We acting, right?"

00:04:16.456 --> 00:04:18.091
[ Laughter ]

00:04:18.091 --> 00:04:20.926
"With the acting, the athlete,
we should find a middle ground."

00:04:20.926 --> 00:04:22.928
-Yeah, there'll be some editing,
right?

00:04:22.928 --> 00:04:25.631
You're like, "Yeah, I'll do
this, and then we'll cut to

00:04:25.631 --> 00:04:27.566
a basket and the ball
will go through." Yeah.

00:04:27.566 --> 00:04:28.735
-You picking up
what I'm putting down.

00:04:28.735 --> 00:04:30.436
-Yeah, I've got a background
in film, yeah.

00:04:30.436 --> 00:04:32.471
[ Laughter ]
-Right, right, right, yeah.

00:04:32.471 --> 00:04:35.675
-Now, I also heard that you were
sort of maybe --

00:04:35.675 --> 00:04:37.143
the cusp is the wrong word
for it --

00:04:37.143 --> 00:04:39.145
that you were actually
considering a career

00:04:39.145 --> 00:04:40.713
in the military
before this all happened.

00:04:40.713 --> 00:04:43.415
-Yeah. So, I actually come from
a military family.

00:04:43.415 --> 00:04:48.320
And I had moved out to L.A.
two years prior to booking this.

00:04:48.320 --> 00:04:52.991
And like I said, I had hundreds
of auditions and didn't book

00:04:52.991 --> 00:04:56.161
anything that was paying
anything over like $100.

00:04:56.161 --> 00:04:58.264
So I was just like,
"I need the money."

00:04:58.264 --> 00:05:01.000
I also, you know,
like the military.

00:05:01.000 --> 00:05:03.502
I thought that I could use
the discipline and, like,

00:05:03.502 --> 00:05:05.938
the training and all that.

00:05:05.938 --> 00:05:11.344
But, like, I had a hip surgery
in 10th grade,

00:05:11.344 --> 00:05:14.847
and they didn't call me back
after they found that out.

00:05:14.847 --> 00:05:18.551
And then I booked this, and then
they actually called me back,

00:05:18.551 --> 00:05:20.720
like, I want to say, like
a month or two after.

00:05:20.720 --> 00:05:23.455
They was like, "Hey, you still
interested in the military?"

00:05:23.455 --> 00:05:24.524
I'm like, "Mm."

00:05:24.524 --> 00:05:26.024
[ Laughter ]

00:05:26.024 --> 00:05:27.759
"I think I'm alright right now."
[ Laughter ]

00:05:27.759 --> 00:05:30.963
"I think I'm good.
Think I'm good."

00:05:30.963 --> 00:05:34.000
But if they listening,
thank you for the offer.

00:05:34.000 --> 00:05:35.401
[ Laughter ]

00:05:35.401 --> 00:05:36.836
I'm good.
-Yeah.

00:05:36.836 --> 00:05:38.737
By the way, whoever turned you
down for that hip right now,

00:05:38.737 --> 00:05:41.741
every week is watching the show
being like, "I blew it."

00:05:41.741 --> 00:05:43.009
[ Laughter ]

00:05:43.009 --> 00:05:45.945
"This guy's hip is fine.
Look at it, he's Magic Johnson."

00:05:45.945 --> 00:05:48.214
-"He could have been
a real good sergeant."

00:05:48.214 --> 00:05:49.948
[ Laughter ]
Man.

00:05:49.948 --> 00:05:52.384
-And you, as we mentioned,
grew up in Michigan.

00:05:52.384 --> 00:05:56.022
So is that Pistons?
Were you a Pistons family?

00:05:56.022 --> 00:05:58.624
-My dad was
a real big Pistons fan.

00:05:58.624 --> 00:06:03.062
But I love Shaq, so I kind of
followed wherever he went.

00:06:03.062 --> 00:06:06.131
But actually, my middle name
comes from Isaiah Thomas.

00:06:06.131 --> 00:06:08.134
-Alright.
-So, like it's spelled --

00:06:08.134 --> 00:06:10.769
I spell it differently
because I didn't know that

00:06:10.769 --> 00:06:14.573
before I changed my stage name.
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:06:14.573 --> 00:06:16.908
-But, yeah, Quincy Isaiah.

00:06:16.908 --> 00:06:18.176
-Alright, well,
that's fantastic.

00:06:18.176 --> 00:06:20.213
That's a very nice tribute
to where you grew up

00:06:20.213 --> 00:06:21.247
and your dad and everything.

00:06:21.247 --> 00:06:22.748
And, man, it is such a fun show,

00:06:22.748 --> 00:06:23.883
and it's so lovely
to have you here.

00:06:23.883 --> 00:06:25.184
Thank you so much
for being with us.

00:06:25.184 --> 00:06:26.652
-Yeah, thank you.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:26.652 --> 00:06:27.920
-Quincy Isaiah, everybody.

00:06:27.920 --> 00:06:30.356
"Winning Time" airs Sundays
at 9:00 p.m. on HBO

00:06:30.356 --> 00:06:32.058
and is available to stream on
HBO Max.

